Pod 
----------------------
apache2-pod.yml
----------------
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: apache2pod  
spec:
  containers:
    - name: apache2
      image: ubuntu/apache2:2.4-22.04_beta
      ports:
        - name: http
          containerPort: 80
          protocol: tcp
...

Use kubectl for creating/querying and deleting the pod on the cluster

1. How to create the pod on the cluster?
kubectl -f create apache2-pod.yml

2. How to see the pods on the cluster?
kubectl get pods -n default
  
3. How to see the information about this pod?
kubectl describe pod apache2pod

4. How to access the logs that are generated by the pod application while running
kubectl logs podName

5. How to get more information about the pods that are running on the cluster?
kubectl get pods -o wide

6. How to expose the pod to the host using port-forwarding?
kubectl port-forward podName hostPort:containerPort
For eg.. to expose the above apache2 pod application to the host we need to run the below command
kubectl port-forward apache2pod 8080:80
  
Then all the traffic that is send on the host machine: http://localhost:8080 would be forward to the pod application that is running on 80 port


7. How to delete the pod?
kubectl delete podName
(or)
kubectl delete -f apache2-pod.yml
